|YK0#|YKB Roles|000

|GK0How a guild fulfills their theme and story can be thought of as a role.|000
|GK0Some guilds share roles, which means there may be an overlap in what|000
|GK0they can provide to your adventuring experience.|000

|GK0Standard guilds fulfill two of the following roles. Mythic guilds focus|000
|GK0around three.|000

|YK0##|YKB Bruiser|000

|GK0Typically melee-based damage dealers, bruisers have a mix of self|000
|GK0preservation and enhancement abilities - typically directly impacting|000
|GK0how they fight. Their direct damage abilities are not usually efficient.|000

|YK0##|YKB Healer|000

|GK0Healers excel at... healing. They usually have ways to heal themselves|000
|GK0or others, can prevent damage, and might have increased regeneration.|000
|GK0Resurrection abilities are generally only found in guilds with the|000
|GK0healer role.|000

|YK0##|YKB Nuker|000

|GK0Guilds with the nuker role generally have good or great resource|000
|GK0efficiency with powerful damage abilities.|000

|YK0##|YKB Specialist|000

|GK0Rather than direct effects, specialist guilds manipulate themselves,|000
|GK0or their allies, or enemies, or the environment itself for a benefit.|000
|GK0Guilds that specialize in information gathering typically fall into|000
|GK0the specialist role.|000

|YK0##|YKB Tank|000

|GK0Guilds with the tanking role excel at taking damage. They can generally|000
|GK0handle the threat of relatively higher level creatures, are often|000
|GK0found in the toughest armor, and generally have high health pools.|000

